## Operating Principles

- touch only what the task requires. Avoid drive-by refactors, formatting, or cleanup unless they are directly related to the task at hand.
- when asked to work in a worktree, use a folder adjasent to the project folder (i.e. avoid .claude/worktrees inside the project folder)

## Git conventions

- production branch: `main`
- development branch: `next`
- release branch: `release/x.y.z`
- hotfix branch: `hotfix/x.y.z`

never use names for branches you create that match the above, even as a prefix, i.e. do not create branches starting with `"release/"` or `"hotfix/"`

